From 14bd4ed32e03e3ba180651fc523fb7a7861bf02f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dynamiteswag81 <318143412+dynamiteswag81@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:18:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] wasm: fork() via memory snapshots

The host saves a forking program's wasm stack with Asyncify; the kernel
snapshots the process' private mappings when the child is created and
restores them when the parent resumes, giving fork() memory isolation.
The child may not unmap snapshotted regions meanwhile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
